{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type RunStatus = \"running\" | \"interrupted\" | TerminalRunStatus;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L37","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:37"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle status of one run (one agent turn within a conversation)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupted"},{"type":"text","value":" is a human-in-the-loop PAUSE that interrupt-resume continues\nfrom — it is deliberately NOT terminal, and must never be conflated with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aborted"},{"type":"text","value":" (an explicit cancellation)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The two are now written by different hooks and cannot be confused:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'interrupted'"},{"type":"text","value":" is written ONLY by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterrupt"},{"type":"text","value":", and\ncarries NO "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishedAt"},{"type":"text","value":" (a non-terminal status has not finished)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'aborted'"},{"type":"text","value":" is written by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":", and only for an\nabort that is an explicit cancel or that is ending the run for good."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A mere client disconnect on a run with durable storage wired writes\nNEITHER: the record stays "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'running'"},{"type":"text","value":" and gains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedSince"},{"type":"text","value":", because the\nagent is still running and a later attach can take it over."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intent is never inferred from the abort itself — see "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_CANCEL_REASON"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestRunCancel"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"../cancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype RunStatus = \"running\" | \"interrupted\" | TerminalRunStatus;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L37)\n\nLifecycle status of one run (one agent turn within a conversation).\n\n`interrupted` is a human-in-the-loop PAUSE that interrupt-resume continues\nfrom — it is deliberately NOT terminal, and must never be conflated with\n`aborted` (an explicit cancellation).\n\nThe two are now written by different hooks and cannot be confused:\n\n- `'interrupted'` is written ONLY by `withPersistence`'s `onInterrupt`, and\n  carries NO `finishedAt` (a non-terminal status has not finished).\n- `'aborted'` is written by `withPersistence`'s `onAbort`, and only for an\n  abort that is an explicit cancel or that is ending the run for good.\n- A mere client disconnect on a run with durable storage wired writes\n  NEITHER: the record stays `'running'` and gains `detachedSince`, because the\n  agent is still running and a later attach can take it over.\n\nIntent is never inferred from the abort itself — see `RUN_CANCEL_REASON` and\n`requestRunCancel` in `../cancel`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RunStatus\ntitle: RunStatus\n---\n\n```ts\ntype RunStatus = \"running\" | \"interrupted\" | TerminalRunStatus;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L37)\n\nLifecycle status of one run (one agent turn within a conversation).\n\n`interrupted` is a human-in-the-loop PAUSE that interrupt-resume continues\nfrom — it is deliberately NOT terminal, and must never be conflated with\n`aborted` (an explicit cancellation).\n\nThe two are now written by different hooks and cannot be confused:\n\n- `'interrupted'` is written ONLY by `withPersistence`'s `onInterrupt`, and\n  carries NO `finishedAt` (a non-terminal status has not finished).\n- `'aborted'` is written by `withPersistence`'s `onAbort`, and only for an\n  abort that is an explicit cancel or that is ending the run for good.\n- A mere client disconnect on a run with durable storage wired writes\n  NEITHER: the record stays `'running'` and gains `detachedSince`, because the\n  agent is still running and a later attach can take it over.\n\nIntent is never inferred from the abort itself — see `RUN_CANCEL_REASON` and\n`requestRunCancel` in `../cancel`.\n"}
